<!--
  Native ClickHouse Prometheus metrics endpoint, production-only.

  Mounted at /etc/clickhouse-server/config.d/prometheus.xml by the
  production compose overlay. Not mounted in the local-development
  stack because there is no scrape target locally.

  ## Listener binding — loopback inside the container

  The endpoint binds to 127.0.0.1 inside the container. This is
  deliberate even though it makes the endpoint unreachable from
  a host-side port mapping (Docker's iptables DNAT routes to the
  container's bridge IP, not its loopback — a host port mapping
  would just hit a non-listening interface).

  The CH Prometheus endpoint accepts **no authentication of any
  kind**. With `userland-proxy: false` on the Docker daemon, port
  mapping 127.0.0.1:9363:9363 keeps it off the public network on
  the host side, but does NOT protect against intra-bridge
  traffic — any other container on the same default Docker
  network can reach `clickhouse:9363/metrics` over the bridge IP
  and pull unauthenticated metrics. Today the prod stack has
  only Caddy + sidecar on that bridge, but the surface widens
  with every future service.

  Loopback binding closes that gap entirely: only processes
  inside the CH container can reach the endpoint. A future
  Prometheus scraper must therefore run either:

   - On the host directly, scraping via `docker exec
     clickhouse curl http://127.0.0.1:9363/metrics`, OR
   - In a dedicated sidecar that shares the CH container's
     network namespace (`network_mode: "service:clickhouse"`).

  Neither path involves the public network. Neither requires
  authentication on the CH endpoint.

  ## What is exposed

  All four CH metric families are turned on:
   - `metrics`: instantaneous counters / gauges
   - `events`: cumulative event counters since process start
   - `asynchronous_metrics`: periodically refreshed gauges
   - `errors`: per-error-code cumulative counters
-->
<clickhouse>
    <prometheus>
        <port>9363</port>
        <endpoint>/metrics</endpoint>
        <listen_host>127.0.0.1</listen_host>

        <metrics>true</metrics>
        <events>true</events>
        <asynchronous_metrics>true</asynchronous_metrics>
        <errors>true</errors>
    </prometheus>
</clickhouse>
